          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Boyle’s Law",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " states that the volume of a given mass of gas varies inversely with the pressure when the temperature is constant.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p99-boyle-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "A gas occupies a volume of 4.0 L at a pressure of 200 kPa. If the pressure is increased to 500 kPa, what is the new volume (assuming temperature is constant)?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.6\\text{ L}$.",
          "worked": "Let $V$ be the volume in litres and $P$ the pressure in kilopascals. By Boyle’s Law,\n$$\\begin{align*}V&=\\frac{k}{P}\\\\k&=200\\times4.0\\\\k&=800\\\\V&=\\frac{800}{500}\\\\V&=1.6\\text{ L}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p99-boyle-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A gas sample occupies 8.0 L at 100 kPa. The volume is compressed to 5.0 L. What is the new pressure?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$160\\text{ kPa}$.",
          "worked": "Let $P$ be the pressure in kilopascals and $V$ the volume in litres. By Boyle’s Law,\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=\\frac{k}{V}\\\\k&=100\\times8.0\\\\k&=800\\\\P&=\\frac{800}{5.0}\\\\P&=160\\text{ kPa}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p99-boyle-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "A gas is compressed from 12.0 L to 9.0 L under constant temperature. If the initial pressure is 80 kPa, find the final pressure.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{320}{3}\\text{ kPa}\\approx106.67\\text{ kPa}$.",
          "worked": "Let $P$ be the pressure in kilopascals and $V$ the volume in litres. By Boyle’s Law,\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=\\frac{k}{V}\\\\k&=80\\times12.0\\\\k&=960\\\\P&=\\frac{960}{9.0}\\\\P&=\\frac{320}{3}\\text{ kPa}\\\\P&\\approx106.67\\text{ kPa}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
